&quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7958&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Elective in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Elective</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"economics-ba-ma__box-6-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;UB Curriculum Capstone&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;UB Curriculum Capstone (UBC 399) is the culminating general education requirement. It is a one-credit course in which you will work in UBPortfolio, with the support of your Capstone instructor, to create a reflective and integrative Capstone ePortfolio based on your UB Curriculum coursework and lived experiences outside of the classroom. All UB Curriculum courses must be completed or in-progress to enroll in and complete UBC 399. Students who drop an in-progress course will be removed from UBC 399 through the add/drop period. Students who resign an in-progress course may not be able to successfully complete the Capstone.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;1&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;All UB Curriculum courses must be completed or in-progress to enroll in and complete UBC 399. UB Seminar is a prerequisite to UBC 399 and therefore cannot be taken concurrently. If you enrolled today in your remaining UBC course(s), HUB will allow you to enroll tomorrow. For questions, email: ubcurriculum@buffalo.edu.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">UBC 399MNT</span><span class=\"box-title\">UB Curriculum Capstone</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">1 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">135 credits</div>\n      </div></div></div></section>"}